@doc """
Standard `Encode` trait declaration.
`Encode<$To>` converts `Self` into `$To`.
The `to: TypeRef<$To>` parameter is a signature-level witness slot and is not
meant to be observed at runtime.
Format-specific value owners can expose source-level aliases that fix the target
type, such as `JsonValue::encode(value)` for `Encode<JsonValue>`.

## REPL
xldr(1)> json =? JsonValue::encode("hello")
xldr(2)> Json::encode(json)
Ok("\"hello\"")
"""
deftrait Encode<$To> {
  # Convert the value into the requested target representation.
  def encode(self: Self, to: TypeRef<$To>) -> Result<$To, Error>
}
